{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"normalizedLaplacianEigenpairs"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"smallest","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1e-8, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxIterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Eigenpairs","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory10EigenpairsV","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/Eigenpairs"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BinaryFloatingPoint","preciseIdentifier":"s:SB"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"smallest","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The number of eigenpairs, in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...vertexCount"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"weight","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The weight of the edge at each position.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"tolerance","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The residual a Ritz pair must reach, relative as described above.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"maxIterations","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The matrix–vector products each Lanczos run may spend; nil for the limits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under Throws."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"return-value","level":2,"text":"Return Value","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The eigenpairs, in order from that end of the spectrum."}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Component by component: each component’s null vector first (eigenvalue 0, components in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order of their least vertex), then the smallest positive eigenvalues of the components"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"merged. On a component of at least 64 vertices, thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reorthogonalization and locking, the null vector projected out, from a fixed start vector:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on σI − M (σ Gershgorin’s bound) while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on M⁺ by shift-invert, each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"product a conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pair is accepted when its residual is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" · λ, relative to itself as for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"algebraicConnectivity"},{"type":"text","text":"; the vectors found are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, and each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value is its vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The dense solver on a smaller"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component, or when k is a third of it or more."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"10) for the basis."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smallest"},{"type":"text","text":" is in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"type":"text","text":", every weight is finite"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and nonnegative, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is at least 1."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"style":"note","name":"Throws","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" when a Lanczos run by shift-invert spends "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":" products"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1,000 when nil), or a conjugate-gradient solve inside it 20,000 + 2n iterations, without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"converging. A run on σI − M hands over to shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"20√n products or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":", whichever is smaller. The dense solver throws as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"laplacianSpectrum"},{"type":"text","text":" does."}]}],"type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/normalizedLaplacianEigenpairs(smallest:weight:tolerance:maxIterations:)-2kxtv"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k smallest eigenvalues of the normalized Laplacian N ("},{"code":"normalizedLaplacianMatrix()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), k"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"= "},{"code":"smallest","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", ascending, each with a unit eigenvector (see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Eigenpairs"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE29normalizedLaplacianEigenpairs8smallest6weight9tolerance13maxIterationsAD0G0VyxGSi_qd__5Edges_5IndexQZXESdSiSgtAA13NoConvergenceVYKSBRd__lF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtoco